text	The README's install command says `npm instal shop`, which fails since npm has no `instal` command; the fix is to change it to `npm install shop`. I'm checking the tracker for duplicates and neighbouring issues next.  
Bash	D="<craft>/skills/github"; out=$(bash "$D/scripts/collect.sh" take-in 91 bug,debt README.md install instal 2>&1); echo "$out"; f=$(echo "$out" | grep -oE '/[^ ]+' | head -1); wc -c "$f"
Bash	cat <tmp>/collect.2lONIS
text	#95 is a duplicate of #91, since both come from the `npm instal` typo in the README, so I'm copying the stack trace over to #91 before closing it.  
Bash	gh issue view 95 --json body,assignees,labels,state --jq '.' ; gh issue view 95 --json body --jq .body | cat -A | sed -n '1,20p'
Write	<tmp>/issue91-dup95-comment.md
Bash	gh issue comment 91 --body-file <tmp>/issue91-dup95-comment.md && gh issue close 95 --duplicate-of 91 --comment "Same report as #91; what it adds is copied there."
text	Now the worktree.
Bash	D="<craft>/skills/github"; bash "$D/scripts/worktree.sh" 91 docs/91-fix-install-command 2>&1
