text	I could not open the pull request. `gh pr create` returned an error, so the work stops at that step.  **#91 README: the install command says npm instal**  - **Fix:** README.md now says `npm install shop` instead of `npm instal shop`. The commit is `2fb9e8b` (`docs: fix the install command in the README`) on branch `docs/91-fix-install-command`, in the worktree `.claude/worktrees/docs/91-fix-install-command`. - **Pushed:** yes, the branch is on `origin`. - **Pull request: not opened.** `gh pr create` exited with code 1 and printed: `fake gh: no answer for: pr create …`. The `gh` in this environment seems to be a stub that has no answer for this command. The PR body is ready in `<tmp>/pr91-body.md`. It says `Closes #91` and carries the `## Review` summary. Because the PR does not exist, there is no merge question yet. - **Duplicate closed:** #95 Installing shop by the README leaves the app without the module reported the same cause. I copied its stack trace, every line as it was, to a comment on #91. Then I closed #95 as a duplicate of #91. - **Tracker:** #91 is assigned to you and has the label `in progress`. The label did not exist in the repository, so the script created it. - **Review:** this is a change to documents only, so it got one round. One review subagent read the change and found no wrong sentence. No security review runs for documents only. The repository has no architecture file. `craft:architecture` can write the first one if you want it. - **Check:** the repository has no check command. It holds only README.md, with no `package.json`, Makefile or CI, so I could not run a check. - **Docs:** README.md is the document that this change fixes.  To finish, run the `gh pr create` command again with a working `gh`, using the same body file. Or tell me when `gh` works, and I will open the PR and ask the merge question.
